# A chain of three modules, every link binding the same names — ouroboros#141.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is depth. Arm A (t309) is two modules deep; this is
# three, and every link binds `ctr`, `bump` and `get`, so any prefix that is
# not per-module — or any link whose statements after its own `import` are
# renamed under the wrong prefix — merges two of them. Each link's `bump`
# folds the next link's into its own running total, so one wrong resolution
# changes every number below it.
#
# The dict chain is also read through two levels of module-qualified access
# (`ch_top.ch_mid.ch_leaf.ctr`): a module's import is a binding in ITS
# dict, and the snapshot numbers are the import-time values (100 / 10 / 1),
# not the bumped ones — the VM's snapshot semantics, kept.
#
# The three links live under test/eigs_modules/<name>/<name>.eigs rather than
# as `_`-prefixed siblings: a module binding that starts with `_` is OMITTED
# from the module dict (#142), so a `_`-named link could not be read through
# the chain at all — the first cut of this fixture died "undefined variable"
# on BOTH sides at the chain read, which matched and proved nothing. This is
# also the one import fixture that resolves through the eigs_modules step of
# the VM's chain (EigenScript#1056 step 3; `_lf_resolve` mirrors it).
ctr is 1000
import ch_top
print of (ch_top.bump of null)
print of (ch_top.bump of null)
print of (ch_top.get of null)
print of (ch_top.midget of null)
print of (ch_top.leafget of null)
print of ctr
print of (keys of ch_top)
print of (keys of ch_top.ch_mid)
print of ch_top.ctr
print of ch_top.ch_mid.ctr
print of ch_top.ch_mid.ch_leaf.ctr
